messages.mods-confirm-encode:
Encode the textures of { $count ->
    [one] one mod
   *[other] { $count } mods
  } ({ $names }{ $more ->
    [0] {""}
   *[other] {" "}and { $more } more
  }) with RimSort's own settings? { $pictures } pictures need encoding, and { $textures } encoded textures get their smallest copies trimmed so Waylith keeps them compressed. This writes .dds files into their folders, Workshop ones included. It can take a few minutes.

messages.mods-unlogged-sources:
Files differ, but the changelog lists nothing new. The code was built from sources that changed since this copy was installed: { $names }{ $more ->
    [0] {""}
   *[other] {" "}and { $more } more
  }. A change to shared build files changes every mod's code this way.

